WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:08.160
From 1995 to 2001, Xena : Warrior Princess&nbsp;
delivered 134 episodes of historical fantasy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:14.560
with a campy twist. In the years since its&nbsp;
finale, it's become a bonafide cult classic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.760
But what has the cast been up to over the course&nbsp;
of the last two decades? We're here to find out.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.880
Though she starts out as a ruthless warrior,&nbsp;
Xena's arc bends towards mercy after an epiphany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.480
leads her to seek forgiveness for the many&nbsp;
crimes of her past. Meeting the gentle Gabrielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.400
who proves to be the perfect&nbsp;
counterpoint to Xena's aggression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.080
certainly helps — with a "good angel" in tow, Xena&nbsp;
wends her way towards something like redemption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.400
over the course of the show. That's not to say she&nbsp;
doesn't do a whole lot of incredibly cool fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.040
along the way, of course. After all, this isn't&nbsp;
a show called Xena: Peaceful Princess. But now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.280
Xena fights for those who can't defend themselves.&nbsp;
Over the course of the series, she takes on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.360
evildoers of all kinds, from the pettiest warlords&nbsp;
to the mightiest gods, all in the name of justice.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.760
Xena might live an active life, but so does Lucy&nbsp;
Lawless, the actor who played her. Since 2001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.880
in television and film, Lawless has racked&nbsp;
up an impressive collection of screen work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.680
She's had significant character arcs on&nbsp;
shows like Battlestar Galactica, The L Word,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.720
Spartacus, Parks and Recreation, and even teamed&nbsp;
up with her old Xena co-star Bruce Campbell in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.480
Ash vs. Evil Dead. As for movies, Lawless has&nbsp;
also been seen in small roles in Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.440
EuroTrip, The Changeover, and a plethora&nbsp;
of television movies. Her next role will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:39.840
be as the voice of Nunchuk in Minions: The&nbsp;
Rise of Gru, slated for a 2021 release.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.360
Xena: Warrior Princess set a high bar for&nbsp;
women's representation onscreen. Take Gabrielle:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.080
Played by Renee O'Connor, she starts her arc on&nbsp;
the show as a babe-in-the-woods type who tempers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.920
Xena's bloodier instincts. But as she learns how&nbsp;
to fight and protect others, Gabrielle grows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.760
changes, and discovers entirely&nbsp;
new facets of herself. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:05.280
Gabrielle becomes a celebrated bard, a&nbsp;
skilled warrior, and an actual Amazon.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.120
While Renee O'Connor has continued working in&nbsp;
television since her 134-episode run on Xena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.240
her career has stayed relatively low-key. O'Connor&nbsp;
has appeared in a number of made-for-television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.760
movies including Last Chance, and the horror&nbsp;
movies Monster Ark and Alien Apocalypse. On&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.160
the big screen, O'Connor has had roles in Ghost&nbsp;
Town: The Movie, Boogeyman 2, Diamonds and Guns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:33.760
and Deadrise. O'Connor's most recent&nbsp;
screen credits are from 2017, when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.640
starred in the drama A Question of Faith&nbsp;
and the family sci-fi movie Watch the Sky.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.560
If you're surprised by the seeming scarcity of&nbsp;
roles on her resume, don't be — it's only because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.600
O'Connor has shifted from working on the screen&nbsp;
to the stage. She's been in productions of Annie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.400
Uncle Vanya, Mary Poppins, and Romeo&nbsp;
and Juliet over the last few years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.600
earning tremendous acclaim along the way. Sure,&nbsp;
it might be weird to imagine sweet Gabrielle as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.160
the fearsome Lady Macbeth, but O'Connor's&nbsp;
skill is more than enough to make it work.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.280
While Lucy Lawless and Renee O'Connor&nbsp;
star in every episode of Xena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:14.560
Ted Raimi's Joxer the Mighty only appears in&nbsp;
43 episodes. This might come as a surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.012
to even the most seasoned Xena fan, such&nbsp;
is the strength of Raimi's performance.

00:03:19.012 --> 00:03:22.480
"Xena!"

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.589
"Yeah?"

00:03:24.589 --> 00:03:27.623
"Joxer the Mighty, at your service."

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.760
Joxer is a wannabe soldier who accidentally&nbsp;
falls in with Xena and Gabrielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.720
who tolerate him in spite of his eternal&nbsp;
incompetence. Joxer eventually falls in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.200
love with Gabrielle, who briefly returns&nbsp;
his affections while under a love spell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.480
But it fades, of course, and Joxer ultimately&nbsp;
marries one of Xena's many lookalikes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.680
with whom he has many children. Because&nbsp;
that's just how things roll in the Xenaverse.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.640
Ted Raimi has gone on to have a booming screen&nbsp;
career since Xena's end. He's worked as a voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.600
actor in Code Monkeys and Buddy Thunderstruck,&nbsp;
as well as landing a list of live-action roles on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:10.000
shows like CSI: NY, Masters of Horror, and Legend&nbsp;
of the Seeker. He also starred in his brother Sam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Raimi's Ash Vs. Evil Dead alongside two of his&nbsp;
Xena co-stars, Lucy Lawless and Bruce Campbell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.000
But film is where Raimi's career has really taken&nbsp;
off. He's been seen in such blockbusters as all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.840
three of his brother Sam's Spider-Man movies, as&nbsp;
well as The Grudge and The Midnight Meat Train.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:34.400
Like Xena, Ares began as a Hercules: The Legendary&nbsp;
Journeys character, played by New Zealander Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:39.680
Smith. Smoldering Ares is a complicated figure&nbsp;
in the Xenaverse — particularly when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.920
Xena herself. It is Ares that imbues Xena with&nbsp;
her violent warrior spirit, and Ares with whom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:52.160
she has a complex romance. He's complicated,&nbsp;
stormy, and played to perfection by Smith.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:56.320
After Smith's time on Xena, he went on&nbsp;
to play the lead role in the TV movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:02.720
Lawless: Dead Evidence and a short film called&nbsp;
The Meeting. Smith was also in the 2002 martial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:08.800
arts fantasy film Warriors of Virtue 2: Return&nbsp;
to Tao but while filming Warriors of Virtue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.640
Smith took a tragic fall from a prop&nbsp;
tower on the set of another film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:19.120
He passed away at the age of 38. His TV movie&nbsp;
Riverworld was released posthumously in 2003,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:24.640
and is his final film. Had he lived, Smith's&nbsp;
next project would have been the Bruce Willis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.040
action caper Tears of the Sun set to start&nbsp;
filming just one month after his death.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.320
As Xena's nemesis Callisto, Hudson Leick is the&nbsp;
picture of malice. A survivor of one of Xena's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.920
past rampages, she lost her village and her family&nbsp;
to the warrior princess' bloodlust. Over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:48.480
course of 18 episodes, Callisto's sole ambition&nbsp;
is to make Xena's life hell whenever possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:53.600
Callisto pretends to be Xena for a while,&nbsp;
committing new horrible crimes in her name to stir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:00.160
up public hatred. She even dies multiple times by&nbsp;
Xena's hand, but is continually brought back. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:06.720
becomes a warlord, a demon, an angel, and even a&nbsp;
goddess over the course of her vengeful journey.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:11.120
Hudson Leick has had a number of one-off roles&nbsp;
in television shows since her stint on Xena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:17.680
including Tru Calling, CSI, Nip/Tuck, Shark,&nbsp;
and Law and Order: LA. She's also been busy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.240
on the film front, booking appearances in&nbsp;
the action thriller Cold Heart, the rom-com&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:28.800
One, Two, Many, and a noirish mystery called Paris&nbsp;
Connections. Recently, however, Leick's career has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.560
undergone a major change. She now works primarily&nbsp;
as a yoga instructor through her company, Healing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:40.080
Heart Yoga, through which she runs retreats,&nbsp;
teaches classes, and even does astrology readings.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:47.440
Karl Urban's Julius Caesar is one of Xena's mortal&nbsp;
enemies. Seriously: Their first meeting ends in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:53.520
him breaking her legs and crucifying her. After&nbsp;
Xena is resurrected, her enmity towards Caesar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.520 --> 00:07:00.080
grows until she finally kills him once and for all&nbsp;
in season four's "The Ides of March." Even that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.600
isn't the end for Caesar, however — he manages&nbsp;
to take the Fates hostage and rewrite reality by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:10.960
using their magical loom. Xena saves the day,&nbsp;
of course, but not before being trapped in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.920
alternate reality in which she and Caesar&nbsp;
rule Rome together as Empress and Emperor.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.240
So what's Urban been up to since Xena&nbsp;
went off the air? The better question is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.760
what hasn't he done? Urban has had significant&nbsp;
roles in some of the biggest film franchises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:30.560
of the last couple of decades, including starring&nbsp;
as Eomer in The Lord of the Rings: The Two Towers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:36.240
and Return of the King, as Bones in Star Trek,&nbsp;
Star Trek Into Darkness, and Star Trek Beyond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:42.720
and as Skurge in Thor: Ragnarok. Urban further&nbsp;
expanded his superhero resume as Billy Butcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:48.880
on Amazon Prime's The Boys, and had a full-season&nbsp;
arc as Detective John Kennex in Almost Human.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:55.200
Urban has also played leading roles in Dredd,&nbsp;
The Bourne Supremacy, Doom, and more. He is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:00.480
to star in the crime drama Cold Providence, which&nbsp;
goes into production in 2021. Karl Urban might not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:05.600
actually be Julius Caesar, but it turns out that&nbsp;
he and Caesar share an unstoppable work ethic.

00:08:07.451 --> 00:08:10.480
Alexandra Tydings' Aphrodite has a&nbsp;
longer character arc on Hercules,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.520
but the 11 episodes of Xena&nbsp;
in which she appears are still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.600
plenty significant. Aphrodite is&nbsp;
something of a valley girl in Xena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:22.080
often used for comic relief and light-hearted&nbsp;
looks into the politics of Mount Olympus.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:26.560
"Hello? The love goddess is off&nbsp;
the clock. I got my own problems."

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:32.480
Her arc turns horrifying, however, when&nbsp;
her brother Ares dies and she undergoes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:37.040
a psychotic break. This results in&nbsp;
the total loss of love in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:42.160
as this emotion cannot exist without&nbsp;
the balance provided by war. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:48.240
Xena comes to the rescue by resurrecting Aphrodite&nbsp;
and Ares, and thus restoring world order.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.960
As a screen actor, Alexandra Tydings has been&nbsp;
fairly quiet since Xena completed its run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:59.200
She has had small roles on the 2001 television&nbsp;
show Sheena, modern classic The Wire in 2008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:05.840
and a handful of other shows and TV movies. From&nbsp;
2015 to 2016, she starred in a number of episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:11.200
of the documentary series From the Mouths of&nbsp;
Babes, in which she discusses her time on Xena.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:16.640
She's also worked as an independent writer,&nbsp;
director, and producer on a variety of projects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:21.360
The Trial of Hanna Porn, her 2015 look&nbsp;
at the struggle for reproductive rights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:25.920
won the Best of Fringe award at the Charm&nbsp;
City Fringe Festival, while Rainbow Bridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:30.000
a short film covering similar themes,&nbsp;
was successfully Kickstarted in 2017.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.800
Many strange characters populate Xena's five&nbsp;
seasons, but Eve has to be one of the weirdest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.240
of them all. Played by Adrienne Wilkinson, Eve is&nbsp;
Xena's daughter, conceived immaculately to serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:48.880
as Callisto's reincarnation after she becomes an&nbsp;
angel. Yes, really. Eve is prophesied to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.960
"bringer of Twilight," who will end the reign of&nbsp;
the Olympian gods. For a huge chunk of Eve's life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.000
she is hidden away and/or on the run, eventually&nbsp;
finding protection with her birth mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.160
Xena. She later becomes a missionary of Eli,&nbsp;
the Xenaverse's loose take on Jesus Christ.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:11.600
Actor Adrienne Wilkinson has kept extremely&nbsp;
busy since her 11 episodes as Eve on Xena. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:16.400
has done a great deal of voice acting for video&nbsp;
games including Star Wars: The Force Unleashed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.760
Command and Conquer 3: Kane's Wrath, The Sopranos:&nbsp;
Road to Respect, and Dead To Rights II. Her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:29.200
television work includes appearances on Undressed,&nbsp;
As If, Angel, ER, Charmed, and Star Wars: The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:34.720
Clone Wars. She's also had small roles in movies&nbsp;
including action caper Raze, and more recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:41.120
appeared in the 2020 horror flick Dreamkatcher.&nbsp;
Wilkinson also wrote, directed, and co-produced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:46.320
the documentary series From the Mouths of Babes,&nbsp;
in which she interviews many of her Xena co-stars.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:52.000
As ruler of the Amazons, Danielle Cormack's&nbsp;
Ephiny is yet another fierce and powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.040
woman of the Xenaverse. While she starts out&nbsp;
on rocky ground with both Xena and Gabrielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.800
over the course of their shared arc, the&nbsp;
women eventually become staunch allies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.680
Ephiny marries the centaur Phantes,&nbsp;
and names her child Xenan after Xena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.760
who performs an emergency c-section&nbsp;
during Ephiny's childbirth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:15.680
Ephiny is tragically killed in battle protecting&nbsp;
her Amazonian tribe, and avenged by Gabrielle.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.400
Danielle Cormack has added an impressive number&nbsp;
of New Zealand and Australian TV credits to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:25.200
name since appearing on Xena. Cormack starred&nbsp;
in young adult fantasy Maddigan's Quest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:30.960
the dramedy Rude Awakenings, crime dramas&nbsp;
The Strip and Underbelly, drama The Cult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:36.640
action-adventure The Legend of the Seeker,&nbsp;
courtroom comedy The Rake, prison drama Wentworth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:41.600
crime procedural Jack Irish, and&nbsp;
rom-com Fresh Eggs. More recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:46.800
she's been working again with her Xena co-star&nbsp;
Lucy Lawless on the crime drama My Life Is Murder.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:53.680
A master escape artist, Autolycus is characterized&nbsp;
by a list of standout skills and personality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:59.520
traits that include his deep sense of justice,&nbsp;
excellent disguises, and campy flair. He only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:05.360
figures in eight episodes, though he has a longer&nbsp;
arc on Hercules, but boy does he make those eight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:11.280
episodes count. Not only is Autolycus an important&nbsp;
ally to Xena and Gabrielle, he brings a wonderful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:15.600
banter-heavy comedy to the show that fans&nbsp;
still relish years after the series' end.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:21.280
The actor who portrays Autolycus, the legendary&nbsp;
Bruce Campbell, needs no introduction. This star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:26.240
of the iconic Evil Dead series — created by&nbsp;
Xena co-star Ted Raimi's brother, Sam — has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:31.840
been a fearsome force in movies and television&nbsp;
for years. Campbell has played significant roles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:38.240
on Burn Notice, The Replacements, Fargo, and&nbsp;
the title role in Ash vs. Evil Dead. Campbell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:43.200
has also compiled an impressive roster of voice&nbsp;
work that includes Rapunzel's Tangled Adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:48.160
and Cloudy With A Chance of Meatballs. He also&nbsp;
made a cameo in the 2013 Evil Dead remake…

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.180
"Groovy."

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.360
...along with a whole host of other&nbsp;
big- and small-screen projects.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.800
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.080
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite shows are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:05.840
